{"name":"Gramps Shoehorn","hex":"#a3896c","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"gramps","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Grandpa, grandfather.","Old man."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["plural of gramp"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/gramps"},{"term":"shoehorn","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A smooth tool that assists in putting the foot into a shoe, by sliding the heel in after the toe is in place.","Anything by which a transaction is facilitated; a medium."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To use a shoehorn.","To force (something) into (a tight space); to squeeze (something) into (a schedule, etc); to exert great effort to insert or include (something); to include (something) despite potent reasons not to."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/shoehorn"}],"entries":[{"title":"Grandparent","blocks":[{"text":"Grandparents, individually known as grandmother and grandfather, or Grandma and Grandpa, are the parents of a person's father or mother – paternal or maternal. Every sexually reproducing living organism who is not a genetic chimera has a maximum of 4 genetic grandparents, 8 genetic great-grandparents, 16 genetic great-great-grandparents, 32 genetic great-great-great-grandparents, 64 genetic great-great-great-great-grandparents, etc. In the history of modern humanity, around 30,000 years ago, the number of modern humans who lived to be a grandparent increased. It is not known for certain what spurred this increase in longevity, but it is generally believed that a key consequence of three generations being alive together was the preservation of information which could otherwise have been lost; an example of this important information might have been where to find water in times of drought."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b2/The_Favorite_by_Georgios_Iakovidis.jpg/330px-The_Favorite_by_Georgios_Iakovidis.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Grandparent","wikidata":"Q167918"},{"title":"Shoehorn","blocks":[{"text":"A shoehorn or shoe horn is a tool with a short handle that flares into a longer spoon-like head meant to be held against the inside back of a snug-fitting shoe so that a person can slide their heel easily along the shoe's basin to its inner sole."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/42/Shoehorn-800.jpg/330px-Shoehorn-800.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shoehorn","wikidata":"Q14983"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a9/A_grandmother_takes_nutrition_classes_%286765977597%29.jpg/250px-A_grandmother_takes_nutrition_classes_%286765977597%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/a/a9/A_grandmother_takes_nutrition_classes_%286765977597%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a9/A_grandmother_takes_nutrition_classes_%286765977597%29.jpg/250px-A_grandmother_takes_nutrition_classes_%286765977597%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A grandmother taking a nutrition class with her grandson","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AA_grandmother_takes_nutrition_classes_(6765977597).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5f/Elizabeth_II_greets_NASA_GSFC_employees%2C_May_8%2C_2007_edit.jpg/500px-Elizabeth_II_greets_NASA_GSFC_employees%2C_May_8%2C_2007_edit.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5f/Elizabeth_II_greets_NASA_GSFC_employees%2C_May_8%2C_2007_edit.jpg/1280px-Elizabeth_II_greets_NASA_GSFC_employees%2C_May_8%2C_2007_edit.jp